# Tenant configuration template. `vantigo add <name>` copies this file to
# /srv/tenants/<name>/.env (mode 600) and fills in the "set by vantigo add"
# block; everything else is the host-wide default a tenant inherits and may
# override by editing its own copy.
#
# Compose reads this file both for ${...} interpolation in compose.yaml and
# as the container's environment (env_file). Both passes interpolate `$`, so
# a literal dollar sign in any value — an SMTP password, say — must be
# written as `$$`. Every key the application accepts is documented in
# apps/server/internal/config/config.go.

# --- Set by `vantigo add` ------------------------------------------------------
TENANT=
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=
# postgresql://vantigo_<name>:<pw>@postgres:5432/vantigo_<name>?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/certs/postgres-ca.crt&pool_max_conns=5
DATABASE_URL=
# Public origin, no path, no trailing slash. Requests with any other Host
# header are rejected with 400, and every mailed link derives from it.
APP_URL=
# Derives every key this process uses (cookie signing, CSRF, TOTP secret
# encryption). Generated once; losing or rotating it invalidates every
# session and every stored TOTP secret.
APP_SECRET=
# Authenticates the one-time first-Owner bootstrap at /setup. Required at
# startup outside development, so it is rotated — never removed — once the
# Owner exists (`vantigo harden`).
BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=
# The cloudflared tunnel's network, so X-Forwarded-For/-Proto from it are
# honoured: real client addresses for rate limiting and audit, and https as
# the request scheme. Detected from the `cloudflare` docker network.
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# --- Per tenant, review after `vantigo add` -----------------------------------
# Business modules this tenant serves; identity is always mounted. energy
# and communications each require customers. Every schema is migrated
# regardless, so a module can be enabled later without a migration.
MODULES=customers,products,energy,communications
# Pin the image per tenant (image tags have no leading "v": 0.16.4). Unset
# follows `latest`, which `vantigo upgrade` moves explicitly — there is no
# auto-updater on the host.
# VANTIGO_TAG=0.16.4
# Container memory ceiling (compose.yaml mem_limit).
# VANTIGO_MEM_LIMIT=1g
# A fresh tenant has no enrolled authenticator, and requiring MFA for
# Owners before one exists would lock the first Owner out. `vantigo harden`
# flips these once the Owner has enrolled from /settings.
OWNERS_ALLOW_INSECURE_NO_MFA=1
# OWNERS_REQUIRE_MFA=1
# Optional: also grants SystemAdmin to the bootstrapped Owner with this email.
# SYSTEM_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# --- Host-wide defaults --------------------------------------------------------
# Host path of the shared PostgreSQL server's certificate (mounted read-only
# into the container as /certs/postgres-ca.crt).
POSTGRES_CA_CERT=/srv/postgres/certs/server.crt

# Application mail: identity invitations and password recovery. Required for
# startup, not merely for sending; until a real relay is configured nobody
# can be invited and no password can be reset. The destination must resolve
# to a public address — the SMTP guard refuses private, loopback and
# link-local ranges, so a relay container on this host will not work.
# SMTP_FROM is a bare address ("no-reply@example.com"), not a display name.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@example.com
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
# "starttls" (default) or "implicit"; "none" is refused.
# SMTP_TLS=starttls

# Attachments for the Communications module, under the tenant's ./data mount.
STORAGE_PROVIDER=fs
STORAGE_FS_ROOT=/app/data/storage

# Graceful drain on shutdown; compose.yaml's stop_grace_period must exceed it.
# SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=30s
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Branding shown by the frontend.
# APP_TITLE=Vantigo
# APP_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@example.com

# Optional OpenTelemetry export (traces, metrics, logs) to a collector on
# the host; off unless the endpoint is set.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4317

# Workforce OIDC and SCIM are per tenant and startup-configured; see
# docs/sso-scim-operations.md. Inject the secrets from a secret store.
# OIDC_PROVIDER=entra
# OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-guid>/v2.0
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SCIM_TOKEN=

# Communications AI drafting, off by default.
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_ENABLED=1
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_API_KEY=
